  "remaining_nonclaims": [
    "A pass proves the launcher's catalog is IOI's and its availability claims are honest. It proves nothing about how many applications exist, how good they are, or whether any of them is operationally bound.",
    "An entry marked unavailable is an honest product state, not a deferred obligation discharged. Binding each entry belongs to that application's own owner record.",
    "The retained census is non-canonical inventory supplying the defect baseline only; the pass condition is recomputed against the canonical catalog, never read from it.",
    "This check never decides whether the launcher is in the P2 profile. That disposition is owned by p2-external-surface-integrity-gate's launcher_disposition, defaults to `included`, and changes only under the recorded removal-conditions test."
  ],
  "rollback_or_stop_rule": "Stop if the launcher's rendered rows cannot be resolved to a single canonical IOI catalog owner, because a launcher with two sources cannot be proven honest about either. The launcher is NOT dropped from the P2 profile because it cannot meet this bar: a failing check and inconvenient, expensive, or slow remediation are both explicitly not grounds for removal, and a failing check closes by repairing the launcher, not by deleting the subject. The launcher's disposition is `included` by default and is owned by p2-external-surface-integrity-gate's launcher_disposition. It becomes `excluded` only under that record's removal-conditions test: a genuine pre-cohort profile decision that removes every sidebar, modal, Home, alias, redirect, and deep-link path to the launcher, updates the P2-reachable closure digest, and passes a negative-reachability verifier. Removal is never an outcome of this check and is never reported as a pass of it.",
  "exit_criteria": [
    "Every rendered launcher row and category resolves to IOI's canonical catalog and IOI-owned taxonomy, every unbound entry is omitted or honestly marked unavailable, every predeclared adversarial branch refuses by name, and the retained literal P2_LAUNCHER_CATALOG_AVAILABILITY_CHECK_EXIT=0 appears exactly once.",
    "The bar is a canonical IOI catalog, IOI-owned taxonomy, and honest availability. Completing the application estate is not part of it: an entry that is omitted or rendered visibly unavailable satisfies this check, and refusing the launcher for not implementing every application it could list is a defect in this check.",
    "This check makes no claim at all only when p2-external-surface-integrity-gate's launcher_disposition records `excluded` under its removal-conditions test. The launcher is out of the P2-reachable closure only when that disposition says so; the absence of a launcher is never inferred from the absence of a finding, and a failing check never changes the disposition."
  ],
